2. What you may do

   a. View and read the Software in this repository.
   b. Use the public demonstration site that the copyright holder hosts.
   c. Anything GitHub's Terms of Service allow for public repositories, such as
      viewing and forking the repository within GitHub's own features.
   d. Anything applicable law allows without a licence, such as fair use or fair
      dealing.

3. What needs written permission

   No other rights are granted. Without the copyright holder's prior written
